        "like": 5
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Just adding to this, they already have plans to implement an 'economy' for creators to sell things, presumably so they can get a cut of it, netting them more money.\nThey're happy to go forward with something like this, but a key stability flaw on their /social/ platform is being shrugged off, when they can get the source for Unity with the right license and fix it themselves.\nI highlight 'social platform' because that's precisely why this issue shouldn't be considered remotely acceptable by the players or the company. People are going to sit in lobbies and socialise, that's the entire point of VRC. The fact that you can't do that without eventually crashing your entire VR setup and having to restart everything is completely ridiculous, fixing it should be up there as a very high priority subject.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
    {
      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "60781616b4d0a10cea2fcb74",
      "author": {
