      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2cc9743e5e4b3102c1074e|full_name}: What Tupper has described is in fact a form of leak. Either the allocated memory in use not being cleared once not needed or the way unity handles things by consuming resources and not being cleared until far later than expected.\nVRChat is actively using Unity functionality to download and load assets at runtime. The only reason I can see how the Unity engine has not addressed this is because of the flexibility that creators get with avatars is so wildly beyond appropriate optimisation for a multiplayer game of this scale that Unity would not care to fix for a tiny game unless it was earning them big bucks. That does not excuse how built in functionality to load any asset in, is not countered by allowing unused allocated resources to be removed once they are no longer in use. It sounds like a basic option that should be available by now in the engine.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
