      "value": "@{5f2cc9743e5e4b3102c1074e|full_name}: Yes actually you can engage Unity to resolve the outstanding issue of not releasing unused memory regarding their assetbundle system or you get the source code to fix the problem specific to your application as do many companies that explicitly use Unity in unique ways not suited for the design methods supported by the game engine. No one said it would be easy but there are ways it can be resolved. Usually though it involves money to Unity, whether that be high earning customer for them or with the source code licensing they may assist.",
