  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-02T12:37:42.089Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, Tupper himself has mentioned that all loaded avatars remain in memory until you switch worlds. This is absurd, especially on high traffic worlds where people come and go in droves without you even physically seeing half of them. You can't stay in a high traffic world too long or you'll inevitably freeze and have to relaunch. Please figure out a way to flush avatar data from memory once a user changes avatar or leaves the lobby.",
